+// texture. A layer's texture re-pointed at a surface imported before (Firefox's tiles and the window's frames
+// alternate between a few surfaces; Firefox's parent looks a tile's surface up again at every swap, a new
+// IOSurfaceRef for the same surface) only re-targets that image instead of importing and binding the dma-buf again.
+// Each entry retains the surface it was made from, so the storage and its ID stay that surface's; an entry no
+// texture uses is let go after 3 s unused, or when the cache is full. Called with sf_cgl_track_lock held.
+#define SF_CGL_IMAGES 96
